=== L1. Theorem L1: traces of F for generic algebraic curvature tensors ===
  C1 and C2sym are built from values Q_ab(h) = F(e_a, e_b; h, h) of the quadratic form only, which the leaf
  condition forces to vanish; C2 and C2' use the bilinear form at h != h' and are side identities.
  [True] n = 3, signature 3,0 (6 free components): C1 = (n+2)|R|^2, C2sym = (n+8)/8 |R|^2 + (n+4)/4 |Ric|^2, hence 8(n+2) C2sym - (n+8) C1 = 2(n+2)(n+4)|Ric|^2  [27 s]
  [True]    side identities (bilinear form, NOT consequences of the leaf condition): C2 = 3/4 |R|^2 + (n+3)/2 |Ric|^2, C2' = (n+5)/4 |R|^2 + 1/2 |Ric|^2, C2sym = (C2 + C2')/2, and the expected asymmetry C2 - C2' = (n+2)/2 |Ric|^2 - (n+2)/4 |R|^2, a nonzero polynomial: True
  [True] n = 3, signature 1,2 (6 free components): C1 = (n+2)|R|^2, C2sym = (n+8)/8 |R|^2 + (n+4)/4 |Ric|^2, hence 8(n+2) C2sym - (n+8) C1 = 2(n+2)(n+4)|Ric|^2  [27 s]
